    <svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <symbol id="i-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="i-down-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 5l13 13M18 8v10H8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="i-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M7.6 12.4l3 3 5.8-6.2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
          <symbol id="i-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 18L18 6M8 6h10v10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
    </svg>

    <section class="hero hero-about hero-services hero-legal hero-case" aria-labelledby="case-title">
      <span class="hbar hbar-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="ah-copy">
        <p class="ah-label" data-reveal>Case study</p>
        <h1 id="case-title" data-speakable>
          <span class="line">Brightwater</span><span class="line">Legal</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="ah-intro" data-reveal data-speakable>A website concept for a legal services firm</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc-index cs-meta" role="group" aria-label="Project details">
        <ol>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Type</span><span class="si-t">Website Concept</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Industry</span><span class="si-t">Legal Services / Professional Services</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Role</span><span class="si-t">Website Design &amp; Front-End Development</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Platform</span><span class="si-t">Systeme.io</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Development</span><span class="si-t">Custom HTML, CSS &amp; JavaScript</span></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark pj cs-open" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>Overview</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="overview-title">Making legal services easier to understand and navigate.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>When someone visits a law firm’s website, they are often looking for answers, guidance, or a better understanding of the legal services available to them.</p><p data-rise>The website needs to communicate professionalism while making information accessible. Visitors should be able to understand what the firm offers, navigate its services, and identify the appropriate next step.</p><p data-rise>Brightwater Legal is a website concept built around that balance: a professional presentation supported by clear content structure and straightforward navigation.</p>
            <div class="pj-actions" data-rise><a class="cta cta-menu" href="None" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>View Live Concept</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-up-right"/></svg></a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="pj-shot cs-shot" style="--ar:16 / 9"><a class="pj-link" href="None" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="assets/img/project-brightwater.webp" alt="Brightwater Legal website concept: the homepage headline reads Family law advice for people navigating separation, divorce and parenting matters in Gold Coast, over a photo of a couple embracing." width="1280" height="720" decoding="async"><span class="pj-hint" aria-hidden="true">View live</span></a><figcaption>Homepage screenshot of the live concept</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-white cs-sec" id="challenge" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Design Challenge</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="challenge-title">Communicating professionalism without making information harder to access.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>Legal websites need to establish confidence, but a formal appearance alone isn’t enough. Visitors also need to find relevant information without working through unnecessarily complicated layouts or dense blocks of content.</p><p data-rise>The design direction focused on three priorities:</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-points"><li data-rise><h3>Professional presentation</h3><p>establish a visual identity appropriate for a legal services business.</p></li><li data-rise><h3>Information clarity</h3><p>organize legal services and supporting content into an easier-to-follow structure.</p></li><li data-rise><h3>Accessible navigation</h3><p>help visitors move through the website and identify relevant information.</p></li></ul>
        <div class="cs-after"><p data-rise>The objective was to balance the credibility expected from a professional services website with an experience that feels straightforward to use.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-amber cs-sec" id="direction" aria-labelledby="direction-title">
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Visual Direction</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="direction-title">A more considered approach to professional-services design.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The visual direction was developed to give Brightwater Legal a distinct identity while maintaining the restraint expected of a legal brand.</p><p data-rise>Typography, spacing, color, and content placement work together to create a consistent presentation. The layout gives important information room to breathe instead of overwhelming visitors with too many competing elements.</p><p data-rise>Key design considerations included:</p>
            <ul class="cs-list" data-rise><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>A clear opening section that establishes the firm’s positioning.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Consistent typography to distinguish headings and supporting information.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Organized content sections for easier navigation.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Deliberate spacing to improve readability.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Consistent visual styling across the website.</span></li></ul>
            <p data-rise>The intention was to make the website feel professional without relying entirely on conventional law-firm design patterns.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark cs-sec" id="development" aria-labelledby="development-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Development</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="development-title">Translating the visual direction into a working website.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The concept was developed on Systeme.io, with custom front-end code used to refine the design beyond standard page-builder layouts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="dm-rows cs-tools"><li><h3 data-rise>Systeme.io</h3><div data-rise><p>Used as the website platform and publishing environment.</p></div></li><li><h3 data-rise>Custom HTML &amp; CSS</h3><div data-rise><p>Used to control the page structure, typography, styling, and responsive layouts.</p></div></li><li><h3 data-rise>JavaScript</h3><div data-rise><p>Used for custom interface behavior where required.</p></div></li></ul>
        <div class="cs-after"><p data-rise>This approach provided more control over the website’s presentation while keeping the project within its existing publishing platform.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-white cs-sec" id="build" aria-labelledby="build-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>What Went Into the Build</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="build-title">Design decisions translated into a working website concept.</h2>
          </header>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-table" data-rise><table><caption class="sr-only">Brightwater Legal: what went into the build</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Implementation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Visual design</th><td>Professional legal-services art direction</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Content structure</th><td>Organized presentation of legal information</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">User experience</th><td>Clear information hierarchy and navigation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Typography</th><td>Consistent heading and body-text hierarchy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Front-end</th><td>Custom HTML, CSS and JavaScript</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Platform</th><td>Systeme.io</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Responsive design</th><td>Layout adjustments for desktop and mobile</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark cs-sec" id="result" aria-labelledby="result-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Result</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="result-title">A professional online presentation built around clarity.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>Brightwater Legal demonstrates how a legal services website can communicate its positioning while making its information easier to explore.</p><p data-rise>The concept brings together a consistent visual direction, structured content, and custom front-end development to create a more considered website experience for a professional services business.</p><p data-rise>It reflects my approach to website design: visual credibility matters, but it should always work alongside usability and clear communication.</p>
            <p class="cs-note" data-rise><em>This is an independent website concept, not a commissioned law-firm project. It does not represent verified client results, legal expertise, or business performance.</em></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <nav class="cs-next" aria-label="More case studies" data-rise>
          <a href="/projects#brightwater-legal"><span class="cs-next-k">All projects</span><span class="cs-next-t">Back to the project overview</span></a>
          <a href="/case-clothing-ecommerce"><span class="cs-next-k">Next case study</span><span class="cs-next-t">Clothing E-commerce</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-amber ab-cta" id="lets-talk" aria-labelledby="talk-title">
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-r" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="ab-in">
        <h2 class="cs-cta-h" id="talk-title">Does Your Website Communicate the Right First Impression?</h2>
        <div class="ab-cta-body">
          <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>For professional service businesses, a website is often one of the first places potential clients go to understand what a business offers.</p>
          <p data-rise>I design and develop websites that make services easier to understand, information easier to navigate, and the next step clearer.</p>
          <div class="ab-cta-actions" data-rise>
            <a class="cta cta-solid" href="https://calendly.com/-aldrichmatthew/15mins"><span>Book a Free Strategy Call</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
            <a class="cta cta-ghost" href="/projects"><span>Explore More Projects</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
</Base>
